# HTML & CSS Standards

The Savitri Timbers website is a premium corporate manufacturing website.

Every implementation must preserve consistency with the existing design language.

---

## HTML

- Use semantic HTML5.
- Maintain proper heading hierarchy.
- Prefer reusable existing structures.
- Keep markup clean and readable.
- Avoid unnecessary wrapper elements.
- Use descriptive class names that match the existing architecture.
- Preserve accessibility.
- Images must always include meaningful alt text.
- Avoid inline styles.

---

## CSS

- Reuse existing CSS variables.
- Reuse existing utility classes whenever possible.
- Minimize new CSS.
- Never duplicate existing styles.
- Keep selectors simple.
- Preserve responsive behaviour.
- Mobile-first where appropriate.
- Preserve existing spacing rhythm.
- Preserve typography scale.
- Preserve the existing color palette.
- Do not introduce new design systems.

---

## JavaScript

- Avoid JavaScript unless absolutely necessary.
- Never replace HTML/CSS solutions with JavaScript.
- Do not introduce frameworks.

---

## Performance

- Prefer lightweight solutions.
- Avoid unnecessary DOM complexity.
- Reuse existing components.
- Optimize images when requested.

---

## Accessibility

- Keyboard accessible.
- Semantic landmarks.
- Maintain color contrast.
- Preserve focus styles.